.J. Stuart. <year>2006</year>. Single I<sub>h</sub> channels in pyramidal neuron dendrites: properties, distribution, and impact on action potential output. <source>J. Neurosci.</source> <volume>26</volume>:<fpage>1677</fpage>&#x02013;1687.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16467515</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib17"><citation citation-type="journal">Liu, Y., and J.P. Dilger. <year>1993</year>. Application of the one- and two-dimensional Ising models to studies of cooperativity between ion channels. <source>Biophys. J.</source> <volume>64</volume>:<fpage>26</fpage>&#x02013;35.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7679298</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib18"><citation citation-type="journal">Ludwig, A., X. Zong, M. Jeglitsch, F. Hofmann, and M. Biel. <year>1998</year>. A family of hyperpolarization-activated mammalian cation channels. <source>Nature.</source> <volume>393</volume>:<fpage>587</fpage>&#x02013;591.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9634236</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib19"><citation citation-type="journal">Michels, G., F. Er, I. Khan, M. S&#x000fc;dkamp, S. Herzig, and U.C. Hoppe. <year>2005</year>. Single-channel properties support a potential contribution of hyperpolarization-activated cyclic nucleotide-gated channels and I<sub>f</sub> to cardiac arrhythmias. <source>Circulation.</source> <volume>111</volume>:<fpage>399</fpage>&#x02013;404.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15687126</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib20"><citation citation-type="journal">Molina, M.L., F.N. Barrera, A.M. Fernandez, J.A. Poveda, M.L. Renart, J.A. Encinar, G. Riquelme, and J.M. Gonzalez-Ros. <year>2006</year>. Clustering and coupled gating modulate the activity of KcsA, a potassium channel model. <source>J. Biol. Chem.</source> <volume>281</volume>:<fpage>18837</fpage>&#x02013;18848.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16670090</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib21"><citation citation-type="journal">Moroni, A., A. Barbuti, C. Altomare, C. Viscomi, J. Margan, M. Baruscotti, and D. DiFrancesco. <y